Phases 1, 2, 5: Cedar auto-remediation, org-wide discovery, real-data dashboard

Phase 1 - Cedar policy auto-remediation:
- New tool-capability trust graph (layers/capability_graph.py) classifying
  WRITE / NETWORK / READ_SECRET / READ_DATA per @tool and flagging dangerous
  capability pairs (write+network HIGH, secret+network CRITICAL).
- remediation/cedar.py generates schema-valid AgentCore Cedar from a finding
  using the documented model (AgentCore::IamEntity / ::Action / ::Gateway).
  It denies the egress leg: AgentCore Cedar authorizes one call at a time and
  exposes no context.tool_sequence, so breaking the chain is the correct and
  schema-valid remediation rather than inventing a sequence attribute.
- remediation/deploy.py wraps the real CreatePolicy API with a dry-run default
  and writes policies/generated/<finding_id>.cedar plus a .json audit record.

Phase 2 - org-wide discovery (discovery.py) via Agent Registry with an
ListAgentRuntimes fallback. A permission failure is reported as "unavailable"
with the real error, never masked as "zero agents".

Phase 5 - dashboard (agentaudit/dashboard/): stdlib-only HTTP backend that
serves only real scan output, plus a UI with the 3-stage pipeline, risk ring,
sortable org-wide table, and Policy & Remediation view. No mock data path
exists in the module. Fixed a real CSS collision where the .bar progress-bar
rule zeroed the width of <header class="bar">, collapsing the header.

Verified: 96 tests green, guard INTEGRITY OK, org aggregation arithmetic
asserted against the live API, UI-served Cedar byte-matches the files on disk.

